israeli troops have swarmed the area  around hebron and nablus in search of  the three missing teenagers  over 200 palestinians have been arrested  so far  most of them members of hamas israeli  prime minister benjamin netanyahu says  hamas is responsible for the boy's  disappearance  but so far no one has claimed  responsibility  the palestinians are cooperating in the  search  the israeli army is coordinating its  moves with the palestinian security  authorities  both sides have an interest in locating  the children  and the coordination is working  the three israeli boys were last seen on  thursday at a busy intersection near  hebron  the largest city in the west bank  young israelis often use bus stops to  hitch rides into town  the crisis has exacerbated already tense  relations between israel and the new  palestinian unity government  made up of both hamas and fatah if the  missing teenagers are not found soon  there are fears that israel will respond  with a military offensive  that could destroy any hope of reviving  peace talks between the two sides
 

